// Geauga County, Ohio — curated directory of meaningful links.
// Single source of truth for the app. Keep entries verified and current.
// Fields: name, category, subcategory, url, description
// Last reviewed: 2026-11-09
//
// Every URL below was fetched and its content checked against the organization
// it claims to be. The Board of Elections, which blocks automated fetching, was
// checked in a browser.
//
// THINGS THAT CHANGED SINCE JULY
//
//   * The Village of Aquilla dissolved in November 2024; its area reverted to
//     Claridon Township.
//   * The old county domain (co.geauga.oh.us) still serves 2020 content; current
//     offices are on geauga.oh.gov, bocc.geauga.oh.gov and office subdomains.
//   * The Board of Elections moved to 12611 Ravenwood Drive; the old
//     boelections.geauga.oh.gov site shows only 2022 content.
//   * Geauga Growth Partnership now links its own site instead of a chamber member
//     listing; the YMCA links the YMCA of Greater Cleveland branch page.
//   * Ravenwood Health merged with Community Counseling Center (Ashtabula) in 2026.
//
// TRAPS
//
//   Chester County PA, Middlefield CT, Burton MI, Russell KS, Newbury MA, Troy OH/NY.
//   geaugatheater.org (Geauga Lyric Theater) now redirects to a gambling site.
//   Geauga Lake (closed amusement park) is skipped.
//
// GEOGRAPHY
//
//   * One city (Chardon, the seat); villages Burton, Middlefield, South Russell and
//     Hunting Valley (mostly Cuyahoga). Fifteen of 16 townships have sites (Munson's
//     site does not load).
//   * Five school districts (Berkshire, Cardinal, Chardon, Kenston, West Geauga).
//     Auburn Career Center and the ESC of the Western Reserve are in Concord (Lake
//     County) but serve Geauga districts.
//   * Shared bodies: Geauga-Trumbull Solid Waste District (Warren), Lake-Geauga
//     Recovery Centers, Lake-Geauga Habitat. Holden Arboretum spans Lake and Geauga.
//
// LEFT OUT
//
//   * County Administrator page, SWCD site, land bank, port authority: none found.
//   * The Review Newspapers: a Mahoning Valley weekly with only partial Geauga
//     coverage.
//   * Punderson State Park ODNR page not found; the state park lodge site is used.

